\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Apple\uc2  Sued Over Handling Of Child Sex-Abuse Material --- West Virginia claims iCloud platform fails to sufficiently block sexual abuse content\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kelly Cloonan \par \uc2 460 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 February 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JB McCuskey, the attorney general of West Virginia, filed a lawsuit against \uc2 Apple\uc2 , alleging the company allowed its iCloud platform to be used to store and distribute child sexual-abuse material.\par \par \uc2 The complaint, filed Thursday in the state's circuit court of Mason County, alleges that \uc2 Apple\uc2 's iCloud platform makes it easier for criminals to maintain large collections of illicit material and enables repeated access and redistribution.\par \par \uc2 The suit claims \uc2 Apple\uc2  has abandoned its responsibility to protect children under the guise of user privacy.\par \par \uc2 The suit focuses on \uc2 Apple\uc2 's move to halt plans for tools aimed at detecting and reporting child sexual abuse material uploaded to iCloud. The plans, announced in 2021, had set off controversy as privacy experts warned governments could abuse the system, using it to surveil iPhones.\par \par \uc2 Federal law requires U.S. technology companies to report detected child sexual-abuse material to the \uc2 National Center for Missing and Exploited Children\uc2 . \uc2 Apple\uc2  has long made far fewer such reports than its peers. In 2023, the company made 267 reports, while \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 's \uc2 Google\uc2  filed about 1.5 million and \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  filed more than 30.6 million.\par \par \uc2 "Rather than implement industry-standard detection tools used by its peers, \uc2 Apple\uc2  repeatedly shirked their responsibility to protect children under the guise of user privacy," the West Virginia Attorney General's Office said.\par \par \uc2 Other lawsuits have been filed against \uc2 Apple\uc2  on similar grounds. In 2024, a group of victims filed a suit against the company in U.S. District Court in Northern California, seeking an award that could total more than $1.2 billion.\par \par \uc2 The company filed a motion to dismiss the case that remains pending. Another suit from earlier that year, filed by a 9-year-old girl in North Carolina, was dismissed last year.\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  said that protecting the safety and privacy of its users, especially children, is key to its mission. The company pointed to its parental controls and features such as communication safety, which is designed to automatically intervene on kids' devices when nudity is detected in messages, shared photos, AirDrop and live FaceTime calls. The feature is turned on by default for children under 18.\par \par \uc2 "We are innovating every day to combat ever-evolving threats and maintain the safest, most trusted platform for kids," \uc2 Apple\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The latest suit seeks statutory and punitive damages as well as injunctive relief requiring \uc2 Apple\uc2  to implement effective detection measures for child sexual abuse material. The lawsuit also seeks remedies mandating safer product design going forward.\par \par \uc2 News Corp\uc2 , owner of The Wall Street Journal, has a commercial agreement to supply news through \uc2 Apple\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260220em2k0002c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
