\par\par \b \uc2 Target Cuts 500 Workers in Revamp\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elias Schisgall \par \uc2 371 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Target\uc2  is laying off about 500 employees as its new chief executive, \uc2 Michael Fiddelke\uc2 , revamps its shopping experience in an attempt to reverse declining sales.\par \par \uc2 The company said it was consolidating the number of districts to streamline its store field structure and better empower store directors, prompting the layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Roughly 100 eliminated roles will come from district offices and an additional 400 will come from \uc2 Target\uc2 's supply-chain sites. No store roles are affected.\par \par \uc2 Target\uc2  said the restructuring would allow for more investment in additional in-store labor and guest-experience training, though it didn't specify how much it would increase in-store investments.\par \par \uc2 The company also announced a leadership shake-up on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Fiddelke, who was appointed in August and officially took the helm this month, has said he wants to improve merchandising, digital capabilities and the store experience.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, he said he was replacing the head of merchandising at the company and bringing in a new chief operating officer.\par \par \uc2 Chief Commercial Officer \uc2 Rick Gomez\uc2  will leave the company, while \uc2 Jill Sando\uc2 , who oversees merchandising for apparel and accessories, home and Fun101, will retire, \uc2 Target\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Fiddelke appointed \uc2 Lisa Roath\uc2 , who previously oversaw merchandising for food, essentials and beauty, as chief operating officer. He named Cara Sylvester, currently chief guest experience officer, as chief merchandising officer.\par \par \uc2 "It's the start of a new chapter for Target and we're moving quickly to take action against our priorities that will drive growth within our business," Fiddelke said. "These leadership changes align the right talent and expertise with key roles, and simplify our structure so we can advance our strategy with greater speed, clarity and accountability."\par \par \uc2 Both Roath and Sylvester will report directly to Fiddelke. They begin their new roles on Feb. 15.\par \par \uc2 Target said Gomez and Sando would stay on for brief periods to support the transition.\par \par \uc2 Target\uc2  added that it was conducting an external search for a chief guest-experience and marketing officer.\par \par \uc2 The leadership shake-up follows Target adding two members to its board last month.\par \par \uc2 Target also reaffirmed its previous guidance for sales, earnings per share and adjusted earnings per share for the current fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260211em2b0001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
