\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  Fires Executive Accused of Bias --- Employee had raised concerns about coming launch of erotic content\b0\par\par\uc2 By Georgia Wells and Sam Schechner \par \uc2 553 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  has cut ties with one of its top safety executives, on the grounds of sexual discrimination after she voiced opposition to the rollout of AI erotica in its ChatGPT product.\par \par \uc2 The fast-growing artificial intelligence company fired the executive, Ryan Beiermeister, in early January, following a leave of absence, according to people familiar with the matter. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  told her the termination was related to her alleged sexual discrimination against a male colleague.\par \par \uc2 "The allegation that I discriminated against anyone is absolutely false," Beiermeister said in a statement in response to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, an \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  spokeswoman said Beiermeister "made valuable contributions during her time at \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , and her departure was not related to any issue she raised while working at the company."\par \par \uc2 Beiermeister served as the vice president leading \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's product policy team, which develops rules for how people can use the company's products and helps design the enforcement mechanisms for those policies.\par \par \uc2 Her ousting came ahead of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's planned launch early this year of a mode that will allow users to create AI erotica in ChatGPT. The planned feature, which would permit adult-themed conversation including sexual topics for adult users, has drawn criticism from researchers at the company who have studied the ways some people develop unhealthy attachments to chatbots, according to some of the people. They have raised the prospect that sexual content could intensify the feelings some people have for the AI personas they view as companions.\par \par \uc2 Members of an advisory council on "well-being and AI" that \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  convenes regularly have also expressed opposition to adult mode and urged the company to reconsider plans to launch it, people with knowledge of those discussions said.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2  has defended the move to expand the permissible content on his platform as part of an effort to "treat adult users like adults."\par \par \uc2 Before her firing, Beiermeister told colleagues that she opposed adult mode and worried it would have harmful effects for users, people familiar with her remarks said.\par \par \uc2 She also told colleagues that she believed \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's mechanisms to stop child exploitation content weren't effective enough and that the company couldn't sufficiently wall off adult content from teens, the people said.\par \par \uc2 She is one of several employees within \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  who have expressed concerns about the launch of adult mode, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  has drawn more than 800 million users each week to ChatGPT in its campaign to build the most advanced artificial intelligence. The company now plans to monetize the engagement of those users with advertising. \uc2 News Corp\uc2 , owner of The Wall Street Journal, has a content-licensing partnership with \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  has kept close tabs on competitors and in December declared a "code red" after the surprising success and growth of \uc2 Google\uc2 's Gemini chatbot.\par \par \uc2 Another competitor, \uc2 xAI\uc2 , has found that offering looser guardrails around sexual content in its Grok chatbot has helped drive engagement.\par \par \uc2 Beiermeister started at \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  in mid-2024 as a part of a wave of hires from \uc2 Meta\uc2  who viewed themselves as trying to change tech companies from the inside, people with knowledge of the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260211em2b0001s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
