\par\par \b \uc2 VW to Raise Pay By 20% in Tennessee\b0\par\par\uc2 By Christopher Otts \par \uc2 395 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 February 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 3,000 hourly workers at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 's assembly plant in Chattanooga, Tenn., would receive raises totaling about 20% over four years under a new tentative deal between the German automaker and the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , according to the union.\par \par \uc2 The agreement jointly announced late Wednesday by the company and \uc2 UAW\uc2  also includes enhanced healthcare benefits and other gains after nearly a year-and-a-half of negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Workers still have to vote to ratify the deal.\par \par \uc2 For the union, the stakes of its pending agreement with \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  are especially high, as it aims to persuade more U.S. auto workers in the South to join the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The union coordinated strikes at several plants owned by Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Jeep\uc2 -Ram parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  -- and won large wage increases -- in 2023.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain sought to quickly follow those victories by expanding union membership inside plants owned by Mercedes, \uc2 Toyota\uc2 , Hyundai and other automakers.\par \par \uc2 "When union workers at the Big Three join together with auto workers in the South, we all win," Fain said after announcing the \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  deal. "This is exactly what our \uc2 UAW\uc2  family at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  has done in this agreement."\par \par \uc2 "This comprehensive agreement will provide meaningful changes for our workforce," \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  spokesman Michael Lowder said. "All these benefits recognize and reward the hard work and dedication our team members give every day."\par \par \uc2 The union made a historic breakthrough at the Chattanooga facility in 2024, making it the only auto assembly plant in the U.S. outside of those owned by the Detroit Three to have \uc2 UAW\uc2  representation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  tried and failed to organize workers at a Mercedes plant in Alabama. Since then, the union's effort has stalled. The Tennessee factory is \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 's only U.S. assembly plant. Workers there assemble gas-powered Atlas sport-utility vehicles and the ID.4, an electric SUV.\par \par \uc2 A worker at the Tennessee plant's top hourly wage would earn about $80,000 in 2026, including an attendance bonus, before overtime and profit-sharing, the company said last September when describing its offer. The deal also gives workers an immediate bonus of $6,550 and job protections, such as limits to \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 's ability to outsource work and commitments for future products at the plant, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260206em260002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
