\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- DOJ Probes Silicon Valley Spy Claims --- Employee at another firm claimed Deel recruited him to get inside information\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rolfe Winkler \par \uc2 358 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has opened a criminal investigation into allegations that Deel, a human-resources company, recruited a spy inside a rival firm, according to documents viewed by The Wall Street Journal, and people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Grand-jury subpoenas were sent out in recent weeks by Craig Missakian, the U.S. attorney for the Northern District of California, the documents show. They seek information related to a spying operation that Deel allegedly ran inside a rival company, \uc2 Rippling\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An Ireland-based \uc2 Rippling\uc2  employee, Keith O'Brien, alleged in an affidavit filed in April that Deel Chief Executive Alex Bouaziz recruited him and gave him instructions for what information to take from \uc2 Rippling\uc2 . O'Brien alleged that other executives were involved in the spying plot, including Bouaziz's father, who is Deel's executive chairman and chief strategy officer.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Deel said the company isn't aware of a criminal investigation but is willing to cooperate with authorities. The company has previously said: "We deny all legal wrongdoing and look forward to asserting our counterclaims."\par \par \uc2 Unsealed court documents allege that an entity tied to Deel transferred $6,000 to an account owned by the wife of Chief Operating Officer Dan Westgarth, and that the same amount was forwarded from the account to O'Brien seconds later.\par \par \uc2 Alex Bouaziz, his father and Westgarth didn't respond to requests for comment. O'Brien's lawyer declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Deel helps companies hire international employees when they are looking to expand by handling paperwork, legal and administrative issues for the new local staff.\par \par \uc2 A round of funding announced in October, several months after the alleged spying was made public, marked up the company's valuation to $17.3 billion from an earlier $12 billion, suggesting that its business has continued to grow in the wake of the allegations.\par \par \uc2 Deel is one of the biggest winners in the portfolio of the venture firm \uc2 Andreessen Horowitz\uc2 . A spokeswoman for \uc2 Andreessen Horowitz\uc2  didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260124em1o0002d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
