\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Louisiana Workers Targeted By Agents\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gareth Vipers \par \uc2 261 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 January 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Federal immigration agents targeted construction workers traveling to the site of a \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  data center being built in Louisiana, according to local law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement agents conducted traffic stops on dump trucks on their way to the site Thursday, the Richland Parish Sheriff's Office said. Two drivers were arrested due to their immigration status, according to the sheriff's office. They were from Guatemala and Honduras.\par \par \uc2 Meta is building a $27 billion data center in Richland Parish, a rural area in the northeast of the state, in a joint venture with investment manager \uc2 Blue Owl Capital\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 ICE agents didn't enter the Meta site "at any time," the sheriff's office said.\par \par \uc2 Meta declined to comment when asked about the arrests. The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Immigration officers have targeted construction sites and manufacturing plants before as part of a wider crackdown by the Trump administration. In September, nearly 500 people were detained at a \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  battery plant under construction in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Gov. \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  has been a vocal supporter of President Trump's immigration crackdown. Landry, a Republican, gave his backing to the deployment of federal troops in New Orleans in December. Representatives for Landry didn't respond to questions Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The campaign, which has involved officers from ICE and U.S. Border Patrol, has seen the deployment of federal agents to cities including Chicago, Los Angeles, New Orleans and Washington, D.C.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260116em1g0001t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
