\par\par \b \uc2 Buffett's Successor To Earn a Top Salary\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Gillers and Theo Francis \par \uc2 459 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The $25 million salary \uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2 's successor is set to receive this year is among the highest paid to an S&P 500 company chief executive in years.\par \par \uc2 Greg Abel\uc2  stepped in as \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2 's CEO on Jan. 1 following Buffett's retirement. A Tuesday regulatory filing reporting Abel's 2026 salary didn't disclose any other pay or perks he might receive. Berkshire has historically not included stock awards in its executive-pay plans, and in a March security filing said that, under a board policy, "Berkshire never intends to use Berkshire stock in compensating employees."\par \par \uc2 Most large U.S. companies haven't yet reported CEO pay figures for 2025, much less 2026.\par \par \uc2 But according to a Wall Street Journal analysis of proxy data from MyLogIQ, Abel's 2026 salary would be the highest a chief executive running a current S&P 500 company has earned in any single year between 2010 and 2024.\par \par \uc2 Including stock and options, as well as pension gains and perks, median CEO pay in the S&P 500 was just over $16 million in 2024, with a median salary of $1.2 million and median total cash payment of $3.5 million. Most of the top 100 best-paid executives received more than $25 million, when stock and other noncash awards are added, MyLogIQ data show.\par \par \uc2 Abel's hefty year-one salary is a departure from how Buffett himself was paid: $100,000 a year, plus the cost of personal security. But Berkshire isn't the passion project of a 95-year-old investing legend anymore. It is more of a regular company now.\par \par \uc2 Considering that Abel is now running one of the 10 biggest companies in the S&P 500, "one would expect his compensation to be commensurate with that level of CEOs," said Bill Stone, chief investment officer at Glenview Trust in Louisville, Ky., which holds Berkshire shares.\par \par \uc2 Abel made just over $21 million in 2024, the most recent year available, nearly all of it in salary. Abel's 2025 pay, along with those of other senior Berkshire executives, will be disclosed in a corporate filing later this year.\par \par \uc2 Buffett and Abel didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Salary was an afterthought for Buffett, whose own Berkshire stock portfolio had been accruing gains since Abel was in grade school.\par \par \uc2 Abel's salary is still a fraction of some recent headline-grabbing pay packages. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  reported paying \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2  $95.8 million in 2024, the year it named him to run the company. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  shareholders in November approved giving \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  $1 trillion in \uc2 Tesla\uc2  stock if he hits certain milestones over the next decade.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260108em180001c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
