\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Jobless Claims Decreased Last Week\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Trevisani \par \uc2 181 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 January 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The number of Americans who filed for new unemployment benefits decreased in the Christmas holiday week, but stayed near a monthslong range, as the U.S. employers hesitate to let go of their workforce.\par \par \uc2 A total 199,000 new unemployment claims were filed in the week through Dec. 27, a decrease from 215,000 a week earlier, the Labor Department said Wednesday. Economists polled by The Wall Street Journal were forecasting 220,000 claims.\par \par \uc2 The high-frequency labor data have fluctuated between 200,000 and 250,000 a week, on a seasonally adjusted basis, for most of last year, as employers held on to existing staff in face of a hazy economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 Continuing claims, a measure of the size of the unemployed population, decreased in the week through Dec. 20, to 1.87 million from 1.91 million a week earlier. Continuing-claims data lag behind initial-claims numbers by a week.\par \par \uc2 The December nonfarm payrolls report, due next week, will shed more light on the state of employment.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260102em120001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
